.TH mnnn-org-cert 1  "mnnn-org-cert 2.15.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-org\-cert \- TLS certificates: the node\*(Aqs site, and each org\*(Aqs for its domains (yours, else ACME / Let\*(Aqs Encrypt, else self\-signed)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn org cert\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
TLS certificates: the node\*(Aqs site, and each org\*(Aqs for its domains (yours, else ACME / Let\*(Aqs Encrypt, else self\-signed)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mnnn\-org\-cert\-status(1)
The certificates in use (or that would be): the node\*(Aqs and each org\*(Aqs, where each came from and when it expires
.TP
mnnn\-org\-cert\-set(1)
Use your own certificate for an org\*(Aqs domains (PEM chain and key). The key is kept in the encrypted store, never logged; it takes priority over ACME and self\-signed
.TP
mnnn\-org\-cert\-clear(1)
Stop using your own certificate for an org (back to ACME or self\-signed)
.TP
mnnn\-org\-cert\-acme(1)
Set up ACME (Let\*(Aqs Encrypt) for the node\*(Aqs domain, or with \-\-org for an org\*(Aqs domains; \-\-off turns it off
.TP
mnnn\-org\-cert\-renew(1)
Get ACME certificates now: the node\*(Aqs, or with \-\-org an org\*(Aqs (needs the challenge reachable)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.15.0
